{ Exercise. Try the questions in the book before reading this line. } 1. Qb7# { Illustrative line. Qb7# mirrors the model. The queen moves from b6 to b7 and checks the king on a8 diagonally. White's king on c6 protects b7. Capturing the queen would move Black's king into an attacked square. The queen covers a7, b8 and its own defended square b7. Those are all three on-board neighboring squares available from a8. The king is in check, so no legal move means mate. } 1-0

