{ Checkmate requires check. Stalemate occurs when the player to move is not in check but has no legal move; it ends the game as a draw. } 1. Qg7# { Illustrative line. Qg7# wins for the same reason as the first lesson: it checks, covers the exits and cannot be captured. Verify that the move attacks the king itself, not just the surrounding squares. Compare Qf7?. The queen covers g8, g7 and h7, so Black has no move. But h8 is not attacked. With no other black pieces or pawns to move, the result is stalemate. A huge material advantage does not override that rule. } ( 1. Qf7 { Alternative for comparison; read the explanation before treating it as a recommendation. } ) 1-0

